# 😄 Emojize - Text to Emoji Converter

## 📌 Description
This Python program converts text-based emoji codes into actual emojis.

For example, users can type `:thumbs_up:` or `:thumbsup:` and the program will automatically convert it into 👍.

This project demonstrates the use of third-party Python libraries to simplify complex tasks.

---

## 🎯 Objective
- Learn how to use external Python packages
- Understand how to install and import libraries
- Work with string input and transformation

---

## 🛠️ Technologies Used
- Python 3
- emoji (third-party package)

---

## 📦 Installation

Install the required package using pip:

```bash
pip install emoji

🚀 How to Run
python emojize.py
💡 How It Works
The program prompts the user for input text.
It scans the text for emoji codes (e.g., :smile:).
Using the emoji library, it converts codes into actual emojis.
The final emojized text is displayed.
🧪 Example

Input:

I love coding :thumbsup:

Output:

I love coding 👍
